+## EasyMovement base FOV (5.2.0+)
+
+The `EasySettings.EasyMovement` assembly is included with this package and activates when
+`com.oreethehat.easy-movement` is at least **5.2.0**. Movement 5.1.0 does not expose this owner API.
+The core Settings assembly has no Movement dependency; Movement does not depend on Settings.
+
+1. Add **EasyMovement / First Person FOV** beside the player's FPS controller and configure its
+   default/crouch/sprint/custom Cinemachine cameras normally.
+2. Add **EasySettings / EasyMovement Settings FOV** beside Settings Controller.
+3. Assign the player's `FirstPersonFov` to `Player Fov`. `Field Of View Provider` is filled when empty;
+   the adapter inspector also has **Use for Settings FOV** for an existing explicit binding.
+4. Edit/apply `Session.Draft.FieldOfView` or use the settings window. No direct output-camera write occurs.
+
+Example: authored walk 60 / sprint 70 plus settings base 80 yields walk 80 / sprint 90. A gameplay
+offset of -15 yields 65 / 75, while the Settings snapshot still contains **80**, not the zoomed FOV.
+The adapter uses `FirstPersonFov.BaseFieldOfView` and `AcquireBaseFovOverride`; each owned lease is
+updated with `TrySet` and released with `Dispose`. It never releases another base request or a
+gameplay offset. Movement owns per-camera clamps and composition. Settings profiles keep their
+existing configured FOV limits; those limits apply to the base, not the final gameplay lens.
+
+Disabled/missing FOV owners produce a specific capability/inspector reason; no fallback writes
+to a Cinemachine output camera occur. Disabling the adapter releases its own leases. After pooling
+and re-enable, Apply reacquires an expired lease. For a different player call `adapter.Bind(playerFov)`;
+binding reads the new owner without silently applying old preferences. Reapply a saved snapshot
+explicitly if that is the intended composition. Provider changes are refreshed through events,
+not by writing lenses each frame. Adapter OnEnable refreshes its already-bound live controller
+immediately when safe, including the initial scene activation order; owner notifications during
+Apply are deferred to a single later refresh.
+
+Advanced owner boundary: `ISettingsFieldOfViewProvider.TryRead(out degrees, out reason)` reads base
+FOV; `Acquire(UnityEngine.Object owner, float degrees)` returns `ISettingsFieldOfViewOverride`
+(`IsActive`, `TrySet`, `Dispose`). Bind the component through
+`SettingsController.BindFieldOfViewProvider(MonoBehaviour)`. Unavailable configured providers remain
+unavailable; an absent provider selects guarded plain Camera FOV. `RefreshFieldOfViewProvider`
+invalidates readback/capabilities without reentering a notification. Startup baseline can follow a
+late-initialized owner until the first commit, provided the draft has no edits.
+
